WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.920
While The Rise of Skywalker answered a number
of the saga's lingering questions, it also

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.400
presented a few of its own.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.910
We can't promise you'll understand every part
of Episode IX after delving into our explanations,

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.690
but we hope we can help you feel at least
a little less confused.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:20.210
The Rise of Skywalker wastes no time in telling
us that Sheev Palpatine, the Emperor from

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.689
the original trilogy that we all presumed
was dead after the end of Return of the Jedi,

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:26.220
is actually alive.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.730
In fact, Palpatine has been pulling the strings
of the First Order this whole time.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.930
"The First Order arose from the Dark Side."

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.820
While we never get a detailed explanation
for Palpatine's survival, we should've known

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.379
better than to assume a fall would kill a
strong Force user like Palpatine, especially

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:48.230
since both Darth Maul and Luke Skywalker survived
pretty serious falls in past Star Wars canon.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.510
After Return of the Jedi, Palpatine slunk
off to the Sith planet of Exegol, where Sith

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.089
loyalists used machines to artificially prolong
his life, similar to how Darth Vader was stabilized

00:00:58.089 --> 00:01:00.989
after his battle with Obi-Wan in Revenge of
the Sith.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.500
Once on Exegol, Palpatine bided his time in
the shadows, waiting until his fleet was strong

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.610
enough to reveal itself.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:12.150
The opening crawl of Rise of Skywalker mentions
that newly-minted Supreme Leader Kylo Ren

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.250
is searching for Palpatine, "determined to
destroy any threat to his power."

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.840
The film then reveals Kylo Ren on the surface
of a glowing red planet, slaughtering a forest

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.490
full of faceless opponents before ultimately
locating a Sith Wayfinder that once belonged

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.570
to his grandfather, Darth Vader.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.800
That Wayfinder reveals the way to Exegol,
where Kylo Ren confronts Palpatine and learns

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.600
the truth of Rey's parentage.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.020
The battle for the Wayfinder takes place on
Mustafar, the volcano planet where Anakin

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.160
Skywalker once dueled his mentor, Obi-Wan
Kenobi.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.810
This time, Kylo Ren is fighting members of
the Alazmec of Winsit, a cult of Vader-worshipers

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.280
guarding his Sith fortress, who also planted
the unlikely forest of irontrees where the

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.890
battle takes place.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:56.760
Unfortunately for the Alazmec, Kylo Ren had
no interest in explaining to them why he needed

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.840
to access the ruins of Fortress Vader, and
found it easier to cut a smoldering path through

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.790
his grandfather's acolytes than to simply
ask permission to pass.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.640
Palpatine assembles a massive Final Order
fleet before The Rise of Skywalker, but it's

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.890
not entirely clear how he does it.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.890
We know that Palpatine was able to channel
the power of all the Sith who had come before

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:20.140
him, that he was cloning Snokes who were also
all presumably strong in the Dark Side of

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.410
the Force, and that he had a network of loyalists
he was able to tap into throughout the galaxy,

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.360
even after his presumed death.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.630
We also know based on the thousands of shrouded
figures in the throne room that either Exegol

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:36.380
had a large native population that was loyal
to Palpatine, or that he was able to physically

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.670
manifest the countless former Sith who resided
within him.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:44.310
Either way, it seems as though Palpatine had
a large and powerful workforce at his decaying

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.350
fingertips, and 30 years of secrecy in which
to build his army.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.441
As for where he acquired the resources to
construct the ships, the Rise of Skywalker

00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:56.751
Visual Dictionary confirms that Palpatine
was siphoning supplies from the First Order

00:02:56.751 --> 00:03:00.680
through loyalists he had embedded within its
ranks.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.560
Following the death of Luke Skywalker at the
end of The Last Jedi, his twin sister Leia

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.340
Organa took it upon herself to train the Force-sensitive
Rey in the ways of the Jedi.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.230
This might come as a bit of a surprise, considering
we never saw Leia receive any Jedi training

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.890
herself, despite indications of her Force
sensitivity throughout the Star Wars films.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:23.390
In The Rise of Skywalker, we learn that when
Leia was younger, she actually did train as

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:28.510
a Jedi with Luke, and essentially completed
her training, even constructing her own lightsaber.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.310
However, on the final day of her training,
Leia had a vision that her Jedi path would

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:36.410
lead to the death of her son, which caused
her to turn away from becoming a Jedi.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:41.350
So while Leia technically isn't a Jedi herself,
she has all the knowledge, training, and capabilities

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.080
necessary to continue Rey's instruction where
her brother had left off.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.680
When the Resistance learns that Palpatine
is alive, they worry that they won't be able

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.319
to stop him, since he's on Exegol, and no
one knows how to get there.

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:58.450
However, Rey remembers that Luke Skywalker
had attempted to find Exegol many years earlier.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.190
While Luke hadn't actually found the Sith
planet, he had tracked the Wayfinder that

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:06.610
revealed its location to a desert planet called
Pasaana, where the trail had gone cold.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:11.240
However, when Rey leads her team to Pasaana,
instead of the Wayfinder, they find another

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.240
clue.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.639
It turns out that many years ago, a Sith loyalist
named Ochi was tasked with bringing the young

00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:21.099
Rey to Palpatine on Exegol, and he carried
a dagger inscribed with the coordinates of

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:22.099
the Wayfinder.

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:26.590
But before Ochi could find Rey, he accidentally
rode his speeder into the sinking fields of

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:32.069
Pasaana, and died buried beneath the planet's
surface, along with the Sith dagger.

00:04:32.069 --> 00:04:36.969
After finding Ochi's Sith dagger, C-3PO reveals
that while he can read the coordinates inscribed

00:04:36.969 --> 00:04:40.949
on it, he is incapable of translating them
for the rest of the team.

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:45.360
As Threepio explains, his programming forbids
him from translating the Sith language under

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.310
any circumstances due to a rule passed by
the Imperial Senate, which may date all the

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.990
way back to the prequels.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.300
As we learned in Episodes One through Three,
Palpatine spent years manipulating the Senate

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:01.849
from within in order to serve his dark purposes,
and eventually dissolved the Senate entirely.

00:05:01.849 --> 00:05:06.330
Knowing this, it makes sense that Palpatine
would've enacted legislation making it impossible

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:11.250
for droids to translate Sith, enabling him
to keep his true identity and master plan

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.629
hidden from his peers.

00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:17.479
When Rey and her friends prepare to leave
Pasaana, Chewbacca gets captured and loaded

00:05:17.479 --> 00:05:22.099
onto a transport by First Order troops, while
a horrified Finn looks on.

00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:26.340
Concerned, Finn runs to tell Rey, and they
both watch as a transport takes flight from

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.250
behind a large rock formation.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:32.710
Rey tries to use the Force to pull the transport
back to the ground, but after meeting opposition

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:37.260
from Kylo Ren, she becomes frustrated and
lets out a surge of energy that causes the

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.410
transport to explode, which she thinks means
that Chewie has died.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.580
Almost immediately, we find out that Chewie
is actually still alive, and is being held

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.689
captive on a First Order ship.

00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:52.030
General Hux mentions that there was actually
a second First Order transport on Pasaana,

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.379
which was the one Finn saw Chewie being loaded
onto.

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:59.199
He must not have seen the second one due to
the rock formations dotting the landscape.

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:03.839
Since Rey, Finn, and their companions left
Pasaana immediately after the transport exploded,

00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:06.840
they missed when the second one containing
Chewie took off.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:12.210
Early on, The Rise of Skywalker sets up the
intriguing mystery of a spy within the First

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.810
Order who is passing crucial bits of information
to the Resistance.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.139
This spy is later revealed to be none other
than the sniveling General Hux, much to the

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:25.150
shock of Finn and Poe, who are completely
blindsided by the First Order officer's turn.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.969
After all, Hux spent the entirety of The Force
Awakens and The Last Jedi fervently opposing

00:06:29.969 --> 00:06:33.249
the Resistance and fighting to advance the
First Order's agenda.

00:06:33.249 --> 00:06:35.110
So what changed?

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:39.469
Based on Hux's explanation to Finn, he still
isn't actually a friend to the Resistance,

00:06:39.469 --> 00:06:42.129
and has no investment in their ultimate victory.

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:46.360
But as much as he hates the Resistance, he
hates Kylo Ren more, and seems to have been

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.240
motivated to switch sides following Ren's
ascension to Supreme Leader.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:55.240
When Ren took Snoke's place, Hux was disgusted
to find his power significantly diminished,

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.189
and seemed to hope that by aiding the Resistance,
he could topple Kylo Ren and subsequently

00:06:59.189 --> 00:07:02.039
seize more power for himself.

00:07:02.039 --> 00:07:05.830
Between the completion of The Last Jedi and
the beginning of production on The Rise of

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:11.839
Skywalker, Carrie Fisher, who has played Leia
Organa since A New Hope in 1977, passed away.

00:07:11.839 --> 00:07:16.740
However, since Leia was still very much alive
in the Star Wars universe, director J.J. Abrams

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:21.479
announced that he would be reworking The Rise
of Skywalker's storyline to incorporate previously

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:25.629
unused footage of Fisher from The Force Awakens
to finish Leia's journey.

00:07:25.629 --> 00:07:30.210
This resulted in Leia being present in the
first act of Rise of Skywalker as Rey's teacher

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:34.279
and the leader of the Resistance, then dying
around the midpoint of the film after reaching

00:07:34.279 --> 00:07:36.949
out to her son one final time with the Force.

00:07:36.949 --> 00:07:41.249
While Leia's ending was largely dictated by
the available archival footage of Fisher,

00:07:41.249 --> 00:07:45.520
her death still provided a bittersweet and
fitting send-off to her character.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.429
Although it appears that Leia only transmits
the name "Ben" through the Force, her son's

00:07:49.429 --> 00:07:52.300
reaction indicates that he received more than
that.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:56.969
Perhaps it isn't only his name that Leia Force-projects
to him, but her feelings of motherly love

00:07:56.969 --> 00:08:01.650
and acceptance, letting him know that even
after all he's done, she still considers him

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.699
her son.

00:08:02.699 --> 00:08:06.919
Leia's last-ditch effort to pull her son back
from the Dark Side pays off, but the effort

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:10.509
of reaching him takes every bit of remaining
strength she has.

00:08:10.509 --> 00:08:14.969
She dies, becoming one with the Force, just
like her brother before her.

00:08:14.969 --> 00:08:19.200
At first glance, it might seem as though Kylo
Ren's transformation back into Ben Solo is

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.479
confusingly abrupt.

00:08:20.479 --> 00:08:25.460
But upon closer examination, Ben's decision
to abandon his Dark Side persona is something

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.849
he's been struggling with for a long time,
both in previous films and in the first half

00:08:29.849 --> 00:08:31.659
of The Rise of Skywalker.

00:08:31.659 --> 00:08:35.780
Before his duel with Rey, Kylo tells her that
he can never go back to his mother.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.349
The Dark Side is the only option available
to him.

00:08:38.349 --> 00:08:42.919
But when Leia contacts him during their duel,
he realizes the truth, he could always go

00:08:42.919 --> 00:08:46.089
back, and the only one holding him back was
himself.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:51.120
Afterward, he imagines his deceased father,
Han Solo, who tells him Kylo Ren is dead,

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:54.720
and counters every argument he can think of
to remain on his dark path.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:59.130
Finally, when it seems as though Ben wants
to apologize for all the evil he's done, Han

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:04.190
replies with his iconic, "I know," communicating
his enduring love and forgiveness.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:08.810
Afterward, Ben tosses his Sith lightsaber
into the ocean, having finally found the strength

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:14.259
to turn back to the Light Side thanks to the
combined efforts of his loving parents.

00:09:14.259 --> 00:09:18.360
Long before the beginning of The Force Awakens,
Palpatine was responsible for the creation

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:22.930
of Snoke, along with an indeterminate number
of identical Snoke clones.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:27.139
Palpatine maneuvered Snoke into a position
of power as Supreme Leader of the First Order,

00:09:27.139 --> 00:09:30.801
and all of Snoke's orders in the first two
films actually came from Palpatine.

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:35.590
While Palpatine was secretly shaping the First
Order, he was also searching for his granddaughter,

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.920
Rey, whom he considered his heir.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.130
He sent out bounty hunters to find her, but
their efforts failed.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:44.750
He didn't know where she was until she started
her Force training under Luke Skywalker.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:50.660
He then tasked Kylo Ren with finding and killing
her, but he never intended for him to succeed.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:55.170
Instead, he hoped his efforts would propel
Rey to lean further into the Dark Side, preparing

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.889
her to take over for Palpatine as Empress.

00:09:57.889 --> 00:10:02.430
Once Rey faced him on Exegol, Palpatine tempted
her to strike him down and take his place,

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.700
just as he once taunted Luke Skywalker.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:09.589
Palpatine claimed that killing him would transfer
his spirit to Rey, along with all the past

00:10:09.589 --> 00:10:13.459
Sith, and they would all rule over the galaxy
as one.

00:10:13.459 --> 00:10:18.149
After Palpatine believes he's won, Rey again
attempts the Force exercise that's been eluding

00:10:18.149 --> 00:10:22.190
her throughout the whole film, trying to channel
the Jedi who have come before her.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:27.040
This time, it works, and Rey is strengthened
by a number of Jedi voices feeding her encouragement

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:29.160
that enables her to face Palpatine again.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.740
If some of those voices sounded familiar,
there's a reason for that.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:37.610
The Rise of Skywalker brings back every significant
Jedi from past Star Wars movies, including

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:43.290
Hayden Christensen as Anakin Skywalker, Ewan
McGregor and Alec Guinness as Obi-Wan Kenobi,

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:49.040
Liam Neeson as Qui-Gon Jinn, Frank Oz as Yoda,
Samuel L. Jackson as Mace Windu, and of course,

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.990
Mark Hamill as Luke Skywalker.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:55.459
Additionally, the scene includes voice actors
from Star Wars animated series who portrayed

00:10:55.459 --> 00:11:01.570
now-deceased Jedi, namely Ashley Eckstein
as Ahsoka Tano, Freddie Prinze Jr. as Kanan

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:07.410
Jarrus, Olivia D'Abo as Luminara Unduli, Jennifer
Hale as Aayla Secura, and Angelique Perrin

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.839
as Adi Gallia.

00:11:08.839 --> 00:11:13.029
The combined strength of Rey and the spirits
of the past Jedi is enough for Rey to reflect

00:11:13.029 --> 00:11:16.570
Palpatine's Dark energy back on himself, killing
him.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:21.130
Since Palpatine technically causes his own
death, his spirit doesn't pass to Rey as he'd

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.459
planned, and the Sith line is ended.

00:11:23.459 --> 00:11:24.459
"No.

00:11:24.459 --> 00:11:25.459
No.

00:11:25.459 --> 00:11:26.459
No.

00:11:26.459 --> 00:11:29.360
You will die!"

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:33.649
Several times throughout The Rise of Skywalker,
characters mention that Rey and Kylo Ren make

00:11:33.649 --> 00:11:38.730
up a "dyad in the Force," a new term we've
never heard in previous Star Wars films.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:43.190
Dyads are extremely rare, and the two of them
together can wield the Force in powerful ways

00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:45.310
that haven't been seen in generations.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.610
Kylo Ren speculates that their unique nature
is due to them being the grandchildren of

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:54.449
two of the greatest Force-users in history,
Anakin Skywalker and Emperor Palpatine.

00:11:54.449 --> 00:11:58.389
When Palpatine realizes that Rey and Ben are
stronger together than either of them are

00:11:58.389 --> 00:12:02.579
separately, he heals his decrepit body by
draining their combined Force energy, then

00:12:02.579 --> 00:12:04.720
tries to weaken them by splitting them up.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.930
Rey is still able to defeat Palpatine by channeling
the strength of past Jedi, but the effort

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:10.779
completely drains and kills her.

00:12:10.779 --> 00:12:15.870
However, Ben is able to revive Rey by transferring
all of his energy to her through the Force,

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.470
which ultimately kills him.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:22.079
Before he dies, though, he and Rey are able
to share a few grateful moments of life together,

00:12:22.079 --> 00:12:25.550
likely made possible by the strength of their
shared bond.

